ence/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122759" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following diagrams represents the vector field $F(x,y)=-\\frac{x}{y}\\,i-|x|\\,j$ at the indicated points?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122759" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-3,1),(2,-1),$ and $(4,2).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the function $F(x,y)=-\\frac{x}{y}\\,i-|x|\\,j\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(-3,1) & =-(\\frac{-3}{1})i-|-3|\\,j=3\\,i-3\\,j \\\\ F(2,-1) & =-(\\frac{2}{-1})i-|2|\\,j=2\\,i-2\\,j \\\\ F(4,2) & =-(\\frac{4}{2})i-|4|\\,j=-2\\,i-4\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now draw our vectors. At each point, we draw the vector associated with that point, placing the tail end of the vector on the point itself. This gives the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/330bf1e0b9b2dff008a3e3878d5b2acba8e14addb637d637874492220cb08f2c.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122759" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a17dc61e240dfa920e72c1d4733b62aa647407f68ff931bf955146fd8a731d34"} {"question" "q-122759" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122759" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/330bf1e0b9b2dff008a3e3878d5b2acba8e14addb637d637874492220cb08f2c.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/81ec06546a0ae47f254f42bfafabcf10c6aa7b776f49c59013c9c198bf1bf89a.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/b014bb3efef5caa6a721173a7470f4600edc8207cae6adc3a77bffe217176e13.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/d150a7172d3a7e876cda685d9b096dd1f8d7d96a3349e355dc26562af75caa47.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/e959a73a075acd0e72e4cfa4edd09fa1710c450286ff574574208d42b2d897c4.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122759" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/330bf1e0b9b2dff008a3e3878d5b2acba8e14addb637d637874492220cb08f2c.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122754" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following diagrams represents the vector field $F(x,y)=(y-2)\\,i+(x+2)\\,j$ at the indicated points?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122754" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-5,3),(0,0),$ and $(2,-3).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the function $F(x,y)=(y-2)\\,i+(x+2)\\,j\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(-5,3) & =(3-2)\\,i+(-5+2)\\,j=i-3\\,j \\\\ F(0,0) & =(0-2)\\,i+(0+2)\\,j=-2\\,i+2\\,j \\\\ F(2,-3) & =(-3-2)\\,i+(2+2)\\,j=-5\\,i+4\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now draw our vectors. At each point, we draw the vector associated with that point, placing the tail end of the vector on the point itself. This gives the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/d6084f0711f728a09a78c9803bec9c6e54274d6d72a2adc2b1547651e0ec702c.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122754" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a17dc61e240dfa920e72c1d4733b62aa647407f68ff931bf955146fd8a731d34"} {"question" "q-122754" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122754" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/040d62d956945b7bb67cae560cda4e09a22be2fa9cd2e5da3f3cc372269f14e4.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/3e9efea8998b1dbaab3cc6d89dce4f99bdb06066e81fcb78a2b3a0e412e2e44c.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/4c9fc6ae3cbbf6fa3d241d3607b26fee1cd0670fde37494638ca90da2b02ecfa.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/80ecb3a560bc23359c3b44baace0523bfe653f0c5a5fee5b5c646d901ade5feb.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/d6084f0711f728a09a78c9803bec9c6e54274d6d72a2adc2b1547651e0ec702c.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122754" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/d6084f0711f728a09a78c9803bec9c6e54274d6d72a2adc2b1547651e0ec702c.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following diagrams represents the vector field $F(x,y)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2})\\,i+xy\\,j$ at the indicated points?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-1,1),(1,2),$ and $(2,-1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the function $F(x,y)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2})\\,i+xy\\,j\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(-1,1) & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,i+(-1)(1)\\,j=-3\\,i-j \\\\ F(1,2) & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,i+(1)(2)\\,j=3\\,i+2\\,j \\\\ F(2,-1) & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )\\,i+(2)(-1)\\,j=-2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now draw our vectors. At each point, we draw the vector associated with that point, placing the tail end of the vector on the point itself. This gives the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/5e9e75b66969e1acd7b1a90a5243a3a496168644a53d541851ba933a5f465553.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a17dc61e240dfa920e72c1d4733b62aa647407f68ff931bf955146fd8a731d34"} {"question" "q-122742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/0c69bb201b98cd3728527c562bf4e92cef3c48adae4e01725c2497a73c97a0af.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/2100cd71f6bbbcc46d3f9f35853f65a9bf0d3f25bf3273db0d244c05221d758d.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/34e44b959282b0bc6c245643329e2b485d3209d89f304cf76c106718120a2f10.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/5e9e75b66969e1acd7b1a90a5243a3a496168644a53d541851ba933a5f465553.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/fc954607d17ae1eadaa0aba8d939343290a5c20f47bf61863cba9c42d9f558c9.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/5e9e75b66969e1acd7b1a90a5243a3a496168644a53d541851ba933a5f465553.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following diagrams represents the vector field $F(x,y)=-2x\\,i+{2}^{y}\\,j$ at the indicated points?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-4,2),(-1,1),$ and $(2,0).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the function $F(x,y)=-2x\\,i+{2}^{y}\\,j\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(-4,2) & =-2(-4)\\,i+{2}^{2}\\,j=8\\,i+4\\,j \\\\ F(-1,1) & =-2(-1)\\,i+{2}^{1}\\,j=2\\,i+2\\,j \\\\ F(2,0) & =-2(2)\\,i+{2}^{0}\\,j=-4\\,i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now draw our vectors. At each point, we draw the vector associated with that point, placing the tail end of the vector on the point itself. This gives the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/58a106f2c0ac7aacd30f7ba8915fd2317a67efb73c1c48fe2d192a5d2576717a.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a17dc61e240dfa920e72c1d4733b62aa647407f68ff931bf955146fd8a731d34"} {"question" "q-122744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/4837efc1a78060b2954fa58b26f35e7b2c6d810ce676959653f8e7eca0b5b476.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/58a106f2c0ac7aacd30f7ba8915fd2317a67efb73c1c48fe2d192a5d2576717a.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/68d33b11d6476a0d35cb7486073e90e2755b46f1d4f935adc5dafb7087b15b99.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/e87092c467b78bfe00651fb9752ed54c7f7784c83612fba2149063eba57952e9.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/f2835e43d43494d3319a6a0db0a411906f0424bdac8830425bad47723010d95c.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/58a106f2c0ac7aacd30f7ba8915fd2317a67efb73c1c48fe2d192a5d2576717a.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/77f88ec1dfbd85b4609800484963d2480e68009eb4ac1f6c9fb620914633ff2a.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (i.e., the $i$ component) is zero for *every* vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nG(x,y)=-i+2\\,j,\\,H(x,y)=x\\,i-y\\,j\n$$\n\n- As we move away from the origin in the vertical direction, our vectors' vertical components (i.e., the $j$ components) get longer. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nK(x,y)=-2\\,j\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $F(x,y)=-y\\,j.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Devel