on/worked-solution" "value" "We notice the following:\n\n- The vertical component (i.e., the $j$ component) is zero for each vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nG(x,y)=j,\\,F(x,y)=-j\n$$\n\n- The horizontal component (i.e., the $i$ component) is positive for each vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nH(x,y)=-i\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $K(x,y)=i.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122634" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a17dc61e240dfa920e72c1d4733b62aa647407f68ff931bf955146fd8a731d34"} {"question" "q-122634" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122634" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "F(x,y)=-j"] ["math" "G(x,y)=j"] ["math" "H(x,y)=-i"] ["math" "K(x,y)=i"] ["text" "None of the listed"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122634" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "K(x,y)=i"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/34aca579b2890586365298c764d051f57d4c80977ee975caad505c923343f90d.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (i.e., the $i$ component) is positive for *every* vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=-i+x\\,j\n$$\n\n- As we move away from the origin in the horizontal direction, our vectors' vertical components (i.e., the $j$ components) get longer. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nG(x,y)=i+2\\,j,\\,H(x,y)=2\\,i-j\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $K(x,y)=i+x\\,j.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a17dc61e240dfa920e72c1d4733b62aa647407f68ff931bf955146fd8a731d34"} 