tions:\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=i+j,\\,K(x,y)=-i-2\\,j\n$$\n\n- As we move away from the origin in the horizontal direction, our vectors' vertical components (i.e., the $j$ components) get longer. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nG(x,y)=5\\,j\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $H(x,y)=x\\,j.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122632" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a17dc61e240dfa920e72c1d4733b62aa647407f68ff931bf955146fd8a731d34"} {"question" "q-122632" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122632" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "F(x,y)=i+j"] ["math" "G(x,y)=5\\,j"] ["math" "H(x,y)=x\\,j"] ["math" "K(x,y)=-i-2\\,j"] ["text" "None of the listed"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-122632" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "H(x,y)=x\\,j"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/st