function that generates the vector field above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-123749" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We notice the following:\n\n- Each vector in our vector field is parallel to the $y$-axis. So, the $i$ and $k$ components of our vector field are zero everywhere. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nH(x,y,z)=i+k,\\,K(x,y,z)=i+{e}^{x}\\,k\n$$\n\n- Moreover, each vector in our vector field is pointing in the *negative* $y$-direction, so the $j$ component of our vector field is negative. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=j\n$$\n\n- Finally, we note that each vector in our vector field has the same length, so the $j$ component of our vector field is constant. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nG(x,y,z)=-{x}^{2}\\,j\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram doesn't correspond to any of the listed vector fields." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-123749" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a17dc61e240dfa920e72c1d4733b62aa647407f68ff931bf955146fd8a731d34"} {"question" "q-123749" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-123749" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "F(x,y,z)=j"] ["math" "G(x,y,z)=-{x}^{2}\\,j"] ["math" "H(x,y,z)=i+k"] ["math" "K(x,y,z)=i+{e}^{x}\\,k"] ["text" "None of the listed"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "q-123749" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "None of the listed"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/state.json" "file_sha256" "55789dd64008110a576bd64e9b964833f20b116226517346849a90a5d2f8031e"} {"question" "e-9440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Draw a diagram that represents the vector field \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y)= -2xy \\, \\mathbf{i} + x^2 \\, \\mathbf{j}\n$$\n\n at the points $(-2,1), (-1,-2),$ and $(1,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/example-9440.json" "file_sha256" "1eb32fc787fd09d58065a0280a4d705e5b47aa8dd01db4686a35d53f7fb10a27"} {"question" "e-9440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the function $\\mathbf F(x,y) = -2xy \\, \\mathbf{i} + x^2 \\, \\mathbf{j} \\,\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(-2,1) & =-2(-2)(1)\\,i+(-2)^{2}\\,j=4\\,i+4\\,j \\\\ F(-1,-2) & =-2(-1)(-2)\\,i+(-1)^{2}\\,j=-4\\,i+j \\\\ F(1,-1) & =-2(1)(-1)\\,i+{1}^{2}\\,j=2\\,i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now draw our vectors. At each point, we draw the vector associated with that point, placing the tail end of the vector on the point itself.